# F-036: parse_proptest.rs::test_semicolon_in_name (DROP pair) — the `;` ends the name, so `injection` is a statement of its own and is rejected. DuckDB 2.0 runs a string's statements one at a time, so the complete `DROP SEMANTIC VIEW dcf_y` ahead of it has already run, as `DROP TABLE t;injection;` drops t in DuckDB itself; the name is not cut into `dcf_y;injection` [syntax]
statement error
DROP SEMANTIC VIEW dcf_y;injection;
----

query I
